file: "packages/core/src/delta/delta_overlay.ts"
doc:
  "What a Delta and a target diagram become once merged: one drawable diagram plus the change type of each element in it.\n"
  "\n"
  "Phase 3 of the delta/diff design\n"
  "(docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-07-delta-diff-design.md). Phases 1 and 2\n"
  "shipped: diff() produces a Delta and the token layer gained a live `roles`\n"
  "table. Nothing draws a Delta. This pillar does.\n"
  "\n"
  "VOCABULARY, fixed for every file in this pillar.\n"
  "  \"target diagram\"  the Diagram being rendered; the `after` state.\n"
  "  \"union diagram\"   the target diagram plus every element the Delta\n"
  "                    reports DELETED, restored from its `before` snapshot.\n"
  "  \"change type\"     a value of archeglyph.content.v1.ChangeType.\n"
  "  \"diff role\"       one of exactly three KEYS of a theme's Tokens.roles\n"
  "                    map: diff_added, diff_modified, diff_deleted. A diff\n"
  "                    role is always a theme's map key, never a parameter.\n"
  "  \"table mode\"      a render in which all three diff roles RESOLVED to a\n"
  "                    value, so those values are painted directly.\n"
  "  \"rotate mode\"     a render in which they did not, so each element's own\n"
  "                    colour is rotated in hue instead.\n"
  "The parameter carrying the three resolved values is named `diffRoles` and\n"
  "has type DiffRoles; it is never called \"roles\", because Tokens.roles is a\n"
  "different thing with 25 other keys in it.\n"
  "\n"
  "No file in this pillar uses \"delta\" to mean the overlay, or \"diff\" to mean\n"
  "the comparison; the comparison is diff() in packages/core/src/diff and is\n"
  "not touched here."

structs: [
  { name: "DeltaOverlay"
    doc:
      "The union diagram, plus a change type for every element in it.\n"
      "\n"
      "The three maps are keyed exactly as `diagram`'s own maps are keyed. For\n"
      "an overlay mergeDelta built, every key present in `diagram.graph` is\n"
      "present in the matching map here, and mergeDelta's own doc is where\n"
      "that is guaranteed.\n"
      "\n"
      "Consumers must still not throw on a key they cannot find. An overlay\n"
      "is an ordinary value that a test or a future caller may construct by\n"
      "hand, and applyDiffPalette states what it does in that case. The\n"
      "invariant is a promise mergeDelta keeps, not one DeltaOverlay enforces.\n"
      "\n"
      "There is no annotations map, and the reason is the content model\n"
      "rather than the Delta message. An annotation is an AnnotationEntry in\n"
      "the STYLESHEET; Diagram carries a Graph of nodes, edges and groups and\n"
      "nothing else. So annotations are not diffable at all, and a Delta could\n"
      "not report one even if content.proto declared an AnnotationDelta, which\n"
      "it does not. What consumers do with annotations is stated by each\n"
      "consumer; applyDiffPalette is the only one in this pillar.\n"
      "\n"
      "A plain data carrier with no methods, and deliberately a class rather\n"
      "than a STRUCT_KIND_INTERFACE struct: every sibling carrier this pillar\n"
      "sits beside -- ResolvedDiagram, ResolvedNode, LaidOutDiagram,\n"
      "DiffOptions -- is a definite-assignment class built with\n"
      "init(new X(), {...}), which is the convention archebuild.yaml applies\n"
      "project-wide."
    fields: [
      { name: "diagram", type: { named: { symbol: "archeglyph.content.v1.Diagram" } } },
      { name: "nodes",  type: { named: { symbol: "Record", args: [{ primitive: CHARACTER }, { named: { symbol: "archeglyph.content.v1.ChangeType" } }] } } },
      { name: "edges",  type: { named: { symbol: "Record", args: [{ primitive: CHARACTER }, { named: { symbol: "archeglyph.content.v1.ChangeType" } }] } } },
      { name: "groups", type: { named: { symbol: "Record", args: [{ primitive: CHARACTER }, { named: { symbol: "archeglyph.content.v1.ChangeType" } }] } } }
    ]
    typescript: {}
  }
]
